lumen (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Native launcher UX, guided software management, and one-click self-updates.
  * Hierarchical category navigation with dedicated Apps, Packages, and Updates surfaces.
  * Universal Escape hierarchy and strict overlay lifecycle management.
  * Complete self-update subsystem with GitHub release discovery, checksum verification, and atomic rollback.
  * Unified async operation task model and cross-thread Qt safety.
  * Expanded system health diagnostics and 160+ automated test suite.

 -- Vaibhav Pandit <vaibhavpandit09@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:30:00 +0530

lumen (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Desktop-grade launcher UX, zero-friction setup, and universal software management.
  * Canonical ActionDispatcher routing all item execution (Enter and mouse clicks).
  * Reliable overlay window lifecycle, focus retention, and taskbar suppression.
  * Universal package management platform supporting APT, Flatpak, Snap, and Pacman.
  * Natural command intent parsing (install, uninstall, update, update all).
  * Interactive and non-interactive PolicyKit (pkexec) privilege escalation.
  * First-class KDE global shortcut setup (lumen setup).
  * Extended health diagnostics and 100+ automated test suite.

 -- Vaibhav Pandit <vaibhavpandit09@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0530

lumen (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Seamless distribution, lifecycle, health diagnostics, and upgrades.
  * Single source of truth versioning and version CLI metadata.
  * Configuration versioning, automatic backup creation, and retention pruning.
  * System health diagnostic command (lumen doctor [--json]).
  * Hardened user-local idempotent installer (install.sh --check).
  * Safe uninstallation with explicit purge mode (uninstall.sh --purge).
  * Automated GitHub Actions release artifact generation pipeline.

 -- Vaibhav Pandit <vaibhavpandit09@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:30:00 +0530

lumen (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Extensibility, custom action scripting engine, and power-user release.
  * Declarative custom actions in ~/.config/lumen/actions/.
  * Safe action execution engine with argument substitution, timeouts, and confirmation guards.
  * Advanced calculator math functions and angle modes.
  * Deterministic physical, time, and data size unit conversions.
  * Offline-capable cached currency conversions.
  * Optional KDE Plasma system tray companion.

